    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** serving as our primary engine, boasting a standout 76.16 efficiency score. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Barnett, where favorable platoon splits and a moderate xERA of 4.56 combine to maximize his production window. While **Corbin Carroll** sits behind him at 69.89, he remains our most dynamic weapon; despite facing a lefty in Gamboa, his elite speed profile forces him into the starting slot, as his ability to manufacture SBs in non-optimal conditions remains too valuable to bench. **Austin Riley** also presents a compelling case at 66.15, as his 19% SP skill bonus and high-upside park factor outweigh the penalty of hitting near the bottom of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was determining how to handle the middle infield, where **Zach McKinstry** barely held onto his spot with a 48.85 score. He effectively edged out our remaining depth players due to his positional versatility and consistent plate appearances, though his sub-50 score keeps him on a short leash. We are keeping a close eye on the 30% rain risk hovering over the **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** matchup; should the game be delayed, we are prepared to pivot to more stable options if the lineups shift. While we would typically look for a boost from **Henry Bolte**, whose 51.98 score is serviceable, he remains a marginal play until he demonstrates more consistent contact against RHP like Wacha. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom** on the IL, as their eventual return remains critical to boosting our sub-optimal bench depth alongside **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Trevor Story**. We are currently navigating the absences of **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** due to scheduling, leaving our active roster tight for this rotation.",
